From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steigr <me@stei.gr>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 10:44:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] 0021: group nodes list view by a configurable label, with
 per-group monitoring metrics

Add --node-grouping-label (env BRIDGE_NODE_GROUPING_LABEL) to bridge,
exposed to the frontend as window.SERVER_FLAGS.nodeGroupingLabel. When
set, the /k8s/cluster/nodes list groups nodes into collapsible
accordion sections keyed by that label's value (nodes missing the
label are bucketed into a trailing 'no value' group); when unset, the
list renders exactly as before.

When monitoring (Prometheus) is available, each group's accordion
header also shows aggregated per-group metrics: pod count, CPU cores
(used / available), and memory (used / available), summed from the
same per-node metrics already polled for the flat list's own
Pods/CPU/Memory columns.
